  "_caveats": {
    "forward_pass_only": "Timed region covers the classifier forward pass ONLY. Flow export, NetFlow record assembly, 39-feature extraction and z-score standardisation are excluded and dominate in a real sensor. Every latency here is a LOWER BOUND on per-flow cost.",
    "batch1_gpu_is_a_launch_floor": "At batch=1 on GPU the measurement is dominated by kernel-launch and synchronisation overhead, not arithmetic. GAP and GCP looking equal there understates GCP's cost; it does not show the cost is zero. Quote the CPU batch=1 cell for a per-flow claim.",
    "cost_gap_is_quadratic_in_C": "GCP is O(C^2 L') covariance plus three Newton-Schulz CxC matmul pairs plus a C(C+1)/2-input classifier, against GAP's O(C L') and a C-input classifier. These numbers are measured at C=32 and license NO claim about wider backbones.",
    "flows_per_second_is_not_packets_per_second": "Line rate is a packets-per-second property of a link. This model consumes flow records, so throughput is comparable only to a flow-export rate; converting it to a link speed needs a packets-per-flow assumption the paper does not have.",
    "see_module_docstring_for_the_other_four": "desktop hardware is not an edge device; PyTorch eager mode is a framework floor a TensorRT deployment would not pay; cudnn.benchmark is pinned to the training default False; warmup removes cold kernels but not sustained thermal throttling."
  },
  "_deployment_point": {
    "cell": {
      "device": "cpu",
      "batch_size": 1,
      "measurement": "compute_only"
    },
    "recommendation": "Quote the CPU batch=1 cell as the per-flow cost of the pooling head, and the CPU batch=512 cell as the batch-scoring cost.",
    "reasoning": "An edge IDS may have no accelerator, so CPU is the conservative deployment assumption. batch=1 is the line-rate case: a detector scores a flow when the flow record closes, it does not wait for 512 of them. On CPU there is no host-to-device copy, so this cell has no transfer-accounting ambiguity, unlike every CUDA cell. The GPU cells are reported for completeness but at batch=1 they measure kernel-launch overhead rather than the pooling operator.",
    "do_not_quote_alone": "The GPU batch=1 cell. It is a launch-overhead floor and will show GAP and GCP as near-identical for reasons that have nothing to do with pooling."
  }
}